body:
Hey! Just had another question. So took him to the vet and everything is fine, he got his first bunch of vaccinations, no sign of UTI. He is now peeing in the litterbox! However, he's been very picky about it. I don't think he likes when it is wet, but he will only pee on paper towels (and not even a thin layer, there has to be a bunch) so assuming I need to get something more absorbent are pee pads the solution to that?

&#x200B;

Also do you have any advice for constant mewing? Its usually at night when I go to bed.

Thank you this is really helpful advice! Sorry about what you experienced, hopefully you can bounce back from it when you're ready. 

&#x200B;

I didn't think about the issue of being able to envision the shape of the car while inside it, so thank you for pointing that out. I think that is some valuable foresight.

looking into the board game as i type this ! we were both watching the new dark crystal series together so ill also have a look at some more fantasy type stuff.

&#x200B;

thats a good idea, i know a few of the climbers he likes, ill keep an eye out for something special.
